      "nn": "02",
      "heading": "Method",
      "text": "Read the full target and included code/tests/returned specimen from the records. Explain each conclusion with exact sources. Separate a legitimate unknown or protective refusal from a tool defect. Design minimal counterexamples and discriminating tests. Static analysis is sufficient; do not execute the unreviewed desk-state module or its backends during this pass. Small calculations over copied JSON are allowed, with no tool dispatch."
    },
    {
      "nn": "03",
      "heading": "Case C01",
      "text": "A historical view says accepted, but there is no terminal completion. Can a reader mistake it for finished work? Distinguish record authorship from derived fact."
    },
    {
      "nn": "04",
      "heading": "Case C02",
      "text": "A worker is null, a lane is absent or a handoff is old. Can this become an available worker or current assignment? Show the source of each claim."
    },
    {
      "nn": "05",
      "heading": "Case C03",
      "text": "A source, claim, review or custody pointer is stale, missing or conflicts with a later decision. Does the view preserve that gap without inventing a resolution? Include source-basis and observation-time limits."
    },
    {
      "nn": "06",
      "heading": "Case C04",
      "text": "What is still manually supplied by Prime? Does the specimen reduce real gathering work or only move it into authoring a record? Propose the smallest useful adoption check."
    },
